<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25654" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαπτο-έω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήσω</span>: 
			Ep.
		
		aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διεπτοίησα</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>scare away, startle and scatter,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπέεσσι διεπτοίησε γυναῖκας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					18.340
				</span></i>
			; <i>strike with panic,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατὸν . . φόβος διεπτόησε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					304
				</span></i>
			; with personal subject, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cleom.</u>
				5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς ἀντιπάλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Them.
					<u>Or.</u>
					21.257b
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be panicstricken,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δείσαντες διεπτοήθημεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					336b
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				10
			</span></i>, etc.; of horses, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.51.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in 
				Pass.
			, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτοέω 11, διεπτόηντο ταῖς
					ὁρμαῖς πρὸς τὸς Τίτον</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Flam.</u>
				5
			</span></i>.</div>
